<Base title="AI Policy · Auvra" description="How Lens AI works on Auvra, its limits and your choices.">
  <section class="wrap page-hero">
    <p class="kicker">Trust & Safety</p>
    <h1 class="h2">AI Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Lens AI is a tool, not a judge of cultural truth.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last Updated: April 2026</p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-bottom:var(--sec)">
    <div class="prose legal">
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
<h2>Contents</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="#section-1">1. Introduction</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-2">2. What Lens AI Does</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-3">3. AI Outputs Are Not Warranted</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-4">4. Human Review and Community Verification</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-5">5. AI Training and Your Data</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-6">6. No Legal or Professional Advice</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-7">7. Reporting AI Errors</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-8">8. Availability and Modifications</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-9">9. Auvra's Role and Limitations</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-10">10. Relationship to Other Policies</a></li>
<li><a href="#section-11">11. Contact Information</a></li>
</ul>
</nav>
<section id="section-1">
<h2>1. Introduction </h2>
<p>
Lens AI is a set of optional, automated tools integrated into the Auvra Platform to assist users with cultural preservation and discovery. This AI Policy explains how Lens AI works, its limitations, and your responsibilities when using it.
</p>
<p>
By using Lens AI, you agree to the terms of this policy. If you do not agree, you may disable Lens AI features in your account settings or refrain from using them.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-2">
<h2>2. What Lens AI Does </h2>
<p>Lens AI can perform the following functions (where enabled): </p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Transcription</strong> - convert spoken content (e.g., oral histories, interviews) into written text </li>
<li><strong>Translation</strong> - translate text between supported languages </li>
<li><strong>Tagging</strong> - generate suggested metadata tags (e.g., culture, region, tradition) </li>
<li><strong>Enhancement</strong> - improve audio and video quality (e.g., noise reduction, upscaling) </li>
<li><strong>Q&A</strong> - answer user questions about preserved content or Auvra features </li>
<li><strong>Artifact recognition</strong> - identify cultural artifacts from uploaded images (where available) </li>
</ul>
<p>
Lens AI is integrated into the Platform but is not required for core preservation features. You may choose to use Lens AI or ignore its suggestions.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-3">
<h2>3. AI Outputs Are Not Warranted </h2>
<p>
AI outputs may contain errors, omissions, biases, or culturally inappropriate suggestions. Lens AI is not a substitute for human judgment, especially for sacred, restricted, or historically sensitive content.
</p>
<p>
Auvra does not warrant that AI outputs are accurate, complete, reliable, or culturally authoritative. You are solely responsible for verifying and editing AI-generated content before publishing or relying on it.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-4">
<h2>4. Human Review and Community Verification </h2>
<p>
Community verification (by elders, experts, or designated community members) is the primary mechanism for establishing authenticity of Contribution Badges. AI suggestions are only that - suggestions. They do not override human decisions.
</p>
<p>
You should not rely on Lens AI alone to determine cultural authenticity, origin, or significance. Always seek verification from relevant community members or cultural authorities where appropriate.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-5">
<h2>5. AI Training and Your Data </h2>
<p>
By default, Auvra does not use your personal content (including private vault content, badge media, or your prompts) to train or improve Lens AI models.
</p>
<p>If we offer an optional program to improve Lens AI (e.g., to better transcribe a specific language or recognize a particular artifact type): </p>
<ul>
<li>Participation will be opt-in only through a separate consent flow, not through this policy. </li>
<li>You may choose which types of content to contribute (e.g., only public badges, only specific languages, or nothing). </li>
<li>Private vault content will never be used for training unless you explicitly move it to a public badge or give separate, informed consent. </li>
<li>You may withdraw consent at any time, but content already incorporated into a trained model cannot be retroactively removed. </li>
</ul>
<p>
Identifiable personal information (e.g., your name, email, account identifiers) will never be used in training data. Aggregated, anonymized metadata (e.g., language tags, content categories) may be used for quality tuning but will not be linked to your identity.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-6">
<h2>6. No Legal or Professional Advice </h2>
<p>
Lens AI does not provide legal, financial, medical, or professional advice. Any information or suggestions generated by Lens AI should be independently verified by a qualified professional.
</p>
<p>
Do not rely on Lens AI for decisions that could affect your legal rights, financial status, health, or safety.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-7">
<h2>7. Reporting AI Errors </h2>
<p>
If you encounter significant errors or culturally inappropriate outputs from Lens AI, please report them to hello@goauvra.com with the subject line "AI Error Report". Please include:
</p>
<ul>
<li>The specific content or query that produced the error </li>
<li>A description of the error or concern </li>
<li>Any supporting evidence (e.g., screenshots) </li>
</ul>
<p>
Your feedback helps us improve Lens AI, but reporting an error does not create a warranty or guarantee of correction.
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-8">
<h2>8. Availability and Modifications </h2>
<p>
Lens AI is provided on an "as available" basis. We may modify, improve, or discontinue Lens AI features at any time, with reasonable notice where practicable. Service availability is subject to the terms of our main Terms of Service (including any provisions regarding downtime, maintenance, or service changes).
</p>
</section>
<section id="section-9">
<h2>9. Auvra's Role and Limitations </h2>
<p>Auvra provides Lens AI as an assistive tool, not as an expert system. We do not guarantee that: </p>
<ul>
<li>Lens AI will be available without interruption </li>
<li>AI outputs will meet your specific requirements </li>
<li>Lens AI will be free from biases or errors </li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="section-10">
<h2>10. Relationship to Other Policies </h2>
<p>This AI Policy supplements, and does not replace: </p>
<ul>
<li>Our main <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> </li>
<li><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> </li>
<li><a href="/community">Community Guidelines</a> </li>
<li>Content Ownership Policy </li>
<li><a href="/copyright">Copyright Policy</a> </li>
<li><a href="/collab">Collaboration Hub Terms</a> </li>
</ul>
<p>In the event of a direct conflict, this AI Policy will govern for AI-related matters. </p>
</section>
<section id="section-11">
<h2>11. Contact Information </h2>
<p>For questions about this AI Policy or to report AI errors: </p>
<p>Auvra Tech Ltd </p>
<p>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@goauvra.com">hello@goauvra.com</a> </p>
<p>Mailing address: No 13 God Time Estate, Igbe Ikorodu, Lagos State, Nigeria </p>
<p>Please include "AI Policy Question" or "AI Error Report" in the subject line, as applicable. </p>
</section>
